os}⁡(4x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{14}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(14\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(1-1)+\\frac{1}{2}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397399 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397400 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397399 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397399 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397399 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397403 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397399 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397399 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397405 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397399 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397399 #edb/ref 1077 "field-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397399 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186397400 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397399 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "41c0a54b-4090-5079-ad72-a367200f1bb8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397400 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397400 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397400 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2236311d-1dcf-5814-8621-6ca58ac136e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592